      {
        "id": "TZ5hC-GJDRC3-B1Y",
        "title": "Develop",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Now you&#x27;ll actually develop your program and do your experiment!</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "SV7XbBVyIDUGiGvw",
        "title": "Text 1",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>The servo just moves, but what tells it how much to move? It needs a &quot;brain&quot;!</p><p>A microcontroller is like a &quot;brain&quot; for the servo. Microcontrollers are like small, very specialized computers. </p><p>Your microcontroller is called micro:bit.</p><p>The code you make in Dataflow is what goes into the microcontroller - it&#x27;s like how your computer &quot;talks&quot; to the the little brain and tells it what specialized tasks it can do.</p><p><strong>To do the experiment, you need to connect your servo to your microcontroller and connect your microcontroller to your computer. </strong></p><p><strong>Then, drag the Dataflow tile below into your workspace </strong>(or open a new Dataflow tile)<strong> and make the program you designed to do your experiment.</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      },
